	doi = {10.1080/02652039709374500},
	abstract = {Mineral oil material was determined in canned foods by on‐line LC‐LC‐GC‐FID. In the edible oil phase of 90 samples of sea foods, concentrations were mostly around 100 mg/kg, but reached 820 mg/kg. The predominant source of this mineral oil material was lubricating oil used for can manufacturing. Mineral oil contamination of the fish was usually a minor source, but cannot be neglected.},
